{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/328927-new-to-hunter-question-about-hellfire-castigation","id":328927,"title":"New to Hunter, Question about Hellfire Castigation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-02T22:53:36-08:00","id":328927,"title":"New to Hunter, Question about Hellfire Castigation","content":"Hello! I'm playing a Lucifuge member in a Hunter game coming up and so, naturally, I've been looking at Castigation. Unfortunately, I've hit a slight bit of confusion with the Hellfire power.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, you make the roll (Dexterity + Intelligence \u2013 target\u2019s Defense) and if you get a success, you hit the target for 1 lethal (or agg if you want to take the damage too). Seems simple. The confusion comes from the sentence for an exceptional success: &quot;No additional effect beyond tremendous damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a pretty standard WoD result for exceptional success, but it doesn't work here. It only applies to powers that have scaling damage, that is damage that is equivalent to your successes. With this power, it specifically says it only does 1 lethal &quot;The fire inflicts one point of lethal damage, unless the target naturally suffers aggravated damage from <br /> fire (like a vampire)&quot; - so what is this &quot;tremendous damage&quot; meant to refer to?<br /> <br /> I've looked online expecting to find an errata or for this to be commonly known confusing passage, but I found no mention of it.<br /> <br /> Is it meant to do a lethal per success? If not, what does the exceptional success refer to? Am I misreading something here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T23:04:10-08:00","id":328946,"title":"","content":"How very fortuitous that I was looking both at this and Mortal Remains tonight.<br /> <br /> As of the latter, it's damage per successes rolled plus Castigation. If you want to keep it as effective as it was, just drop the Castigation part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T00:53:29-08:00","id":328983,"title":"","content":"As ArcaneArts said. Even if you're not using the rest of the Second Edition update stuff in Mortal Remains, Hellfire ought to be doing a point of damage per success to be competitive with other means of inflicting damage, and the wording of the exceptional success result seems to indicate that the writer had that in mind and just failed to communicate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T07:01:00-08:00","id":329179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/328927-new-to-hunter-question-about-hellfire-castigation?p=328946#post328946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How very fortuitous that I was looking both at this and Mortal Remains tonight.<br /> <br /> As of the latter, it's damage per successes rolled plus Castigation. If you want to keep it as effective as it was, just drop the Castigation part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, does Mortal Remains have a 'fix' listed for it? My GM has a copy and I didn't actually have a look.<br /> <br /> It certainly does seem to be written to do a point of damage per success. Thanks to the both of you. Any other opinions or proof is welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}